# --- trained artifacts -------------------------------------------------------
# Tracked intentionally: the dataset and every trained model are committed under artifacts/, so
# an evaluator can run the full stack immediately with no data generation or training step.
# Everything here is still reproducible byte-for-byte from source under seed 42 -- see README
# section 3 to regenerate instead of trusting the committed copy.

# Belt-and-braces: guards against a *different* model-binary format landing elsewhere in the tree.
# This project's models and dataset are JSON/Parquet, both intentionally tracked above, so the two
# dataset files are named explicitly and excluded from the parquet rule below.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.lgb
*.parquet
!artifacts/dataset/events.parquet
!artifacts/dataset/labels.parquet
*.feather
*.h5

# --- notebooks ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- frontend ---
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Generated at the repository root by `python -m evaluation.report`. The authored deliverable is
# DETAILED_REPORT.md; this is a machine-written summary of the metrics artifacts, so it is not
# tracked. Anchored with a leading slash so it does not also exclude docs/report/REPORT.md, which
# is a committed submission artifact.
/REPORT.md

# --- development-only notes, deliberately not part of the submission ---
Hackathon_Implementation_Plan.md
PROJECT_STATE.md
AI_Powered_Behavioral_Anomaly_Detection_Hackathon_Details.md

# --- editors / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
